chip ym2608
clock 7987200
samples 36000
mem adpcm-b opn-b.bin
fidelity min
# ADPCM-B from memory, at the minimum fidelity: the sine played once with
# end of sample, its status bits read through the extended status, masked
# by the flag control at 0x110, the IRQ enable at 0x29, a flag reset
# through 0x110's top bit, repeat over the ramp, both pans, the level, a
# playback at 8-bit DRAM granularity, and the reset bit.
0 w 0 29 1 84 2 10 3 00  # the EOS IRQ on, nothing masked
0 w 2 01 3 c0 2 02 3 00 2 03 3 00 2 04 3 ff 2 05 3 00 2 09 3 00 2 0a 3 c0 2 0b 3 c0 2 00 3 a0  # the sine's first 1 KB, once
100 r 2
550 r 2
1000 r 2
1450 r 2
1900 r 2
2350 r 2
2800 r 2
3250 r 2
3700 r 2
4150 r 2
4600 r 2
5050 r 2
5500 r 2
5950 r 2
6000 w 2 10 3 04  # mask EOS
6000 r 2
6400 r 2
6850 r 2
7300 r 2
7750 r 2
8000 w 2 10 3 80  # reset the flags
8000 r 2
8200 r 2
8650 r 2
9000 w 2 10 3 00 0 29 1 8c  # BRDY too
9100 r 2
9550 r 2
10000 r 2
10450 r 2
10900 r 2
11350 r 2
11800 r 2
12000 w 2 01 3 80 2 02 3 00 2 03 3 04 2 04 3 7f 2 05 3 05 2 0a 3 a0 2 00 3 b0  # the ramp, repeating, left only
18000 w 2 01 3 40 2 0b 3 ff  # right only, full level
18000 r 2
22000 w 2 01 3 c2 2 02 3 80 2 03 3 01 2 04 3 ff 2 05 3 01 2 09 3 80 2 0a 3 40 2 00 3 a0  # 8-bit DRAM: 32-byte units, the chirp
22100 r 2
23600 r 2
25100 r 2
26600 r 2
28100 r 2
29600 r 2
30000 w 2 00 3 01  # reset
30000 r 2
31000 w 2 01 3 c0 2 02 3 00 2 03 3 08 2 04 3 ff 2 05 3 0b 2 00 3 a0  # the square, loud enough to clamp
31100 r 2
32600 r 2
34100 r 2
35600 r 2
